## Each element once, by `alike`: the first of each, in order.
##
## # Parameters
## - `alike`: whether two elements count as the same.
## - `xs`: the list.
##
## # Returns
## A new list with no two alike.
##
## # Examples
## ```pyking
## import list
## print(list.unique_by(lam (a, b). a % 3 == b % 3, [1, 2, 4, 3, 5]))
## ```
## ```stdout
## [1, 2, 3]
## ```
public def unique_by(alike: (a, a) -> Bool, xs: [a]) -> [a]:
    out = dynarray()
    for x in xs:
        if not any(lam y. alike(x, y), out):
            push(out, x)
    list(out)


